In article <1ti3ac$gll@corax.udac.uu.se> hansen@corax.udac.uu.se (Hans Engstr|m) writes:
>
>Here are some misc. questions which may or may not contain some spoilers...

Spoilers ahoy!


>1. Is there an option to get Nethack to keep your savefile at another
>   directory, instead of the regular save-directory.

For what format?

Mine (Atari) has an options file you can edit.  Check your documentation.

>2. How do you zap a wand ( i.e. a wand of digging ) down ? I have tried
>   the down-arrow key but without success.

It's ">".  Likewise, up is "<".  Not much use for zapping up though.

>3. What is a horn of plenty ? What happens when you apply it ?

It spits out food.  I found one only once.  I guess they're pretty
rare?  Saves you from carrying around a lot of food though.  

>5. What are the effects of a amulet of change ?

Makes you polymorph randomly.  It's usually cursed when you pick it
up.  A good rule of thumb is to check to see if a ringg or amulet is
cursed or not before you put it on.  NEVER put on a cursed amulet or
ring before you find out.  You can find out in various ways, the
easiest being an altar, or your pet.

>6. I have seen ascension posts with dex, wis and int greater than 18.
>   My Valkyrie can't seem to get more than 18 ( quaffing blessed potion
>   of Gain Ability ). Why? Is it class-dependant?

Gauntlets of Dexterity and Helm of Brilliance.  They will raise you a
point for each bonus point on the armor.  I don't know how to get
higher intelligence, since I think Brilliance will only affect your
Wisdom.

>8. When I #sit on thrones they usually vanish in a puff of smoke. Is that
>   normal or is it more to it than that? Should I wait some turns between
>   sitting on them?

This depends on your luck.  You will usually not get anything good
unless you're "lucky."  This is one instance where luckstones come in
real handy.  You cann be granted lots of good stuff, including genociding
a creature, random blessings of your items, getting a peek at your
intrinsic list, and even wishes.  Be sure to drop your gold before you
sit down!

